<title>USA: Castle Rock to cut half its workforce-report.</title>
<headline>Castle Rock to cut half its workforce-report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Castle Rock Entertainment plans to lay off over half its employees over the next few weeks, cutting as many as 80 jobs, Daily Variety said on Monday, quoting the company.</p>
<p>Job cuts were seen in departments which overlapped with Castle Rock's parent studio, Time Warner Inc 's Warner Bros, the report said.</p>
<p>Marketing, publicity, physical production, administration and international distribution would be hit the hardest, Daily Variety said, citing sources.</p>
<p>Castle Rock would keep its production and development divisions, but would have to make five pictures per year, Variety said.</p>
<p>Time Warner was not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
